# Serena + Symbol Navigation (UMBRA-CORE)

Mimir V2 remains mandatory for coding tasks (see `02-mimir-v2.mdc`). Serena provides symbol-aware inspection when application code exists.

## When to use Serena

- Exact symbol lookup, references, renames, and surgical edits
- Prefer after Mimir context compile / hybrid search bounds the area
- Greenfield: Serena project is configured as `UMBRA-CORE` (`.serena/project.yml`); languages list may be empty until stack is chosen

## Rules

- Prefer precise symbol lookup over broad search-and-replace
- Preserve existing repository conventions unless they conflict with `.agent/PROJECT_GOAL.md` or the active task
- If Serena is unavailable or languages are empty, fall back to targeted reads, `rg`, and compiler diagnostics — report the limitation plainly

## Governance reminder

Read `PROJECT_GOAL.md`, `PROJECT_PROFILE.md`, and `CURRENT.md` every task. Follow the Mimir V2 lifecycle. Do not edit `.agent/RECORD.md`.
